  "implemented": [
    "ProductionRulePlatform overrides RuleCookieHost and all five operations reuse task.session.cookies. A retained host checks environment, task deadline/cancellation and session lifetime before touching the same jar monitor.",
    "Original setCookie means replace textual state; original replaceCookie means merge named nonblank values. Their new dedicated internal jar operations do not change the existing HTTP Set-Cookie/mainJs methods with similar names.",
    "Input text uses the first equals sign, trims ASCII boundary whitespace, ignores blank/malformed pairs, preserves literal null, later duplicates win. Complete URI/name/value validation occurs before mutation; representability errors stay typed UnsupportedRuleCapability.",
    "Merge changes only the value field of matching existing JDK cookies under the shared lock; same-name different path/domain objects retain security flags, HttpOnly, domain, path, maxAge, creation metadata and header order. Only genuinely new names receive version-0 host-root cookies.",
    "get(url,key) delegates visibility to CookieManager then maps its exact per-cookie rendering to logical values. This handles JDK RFC2965 quoted values without exposing Secure/path/port-hidden cookie values or $Path/$Version as logical keys.",
    "No new CookieManager/cache/persistent state, native HTTP fallback, original rule parser replacement, App route switch, HTTP transport API change, or cleanup of another session."
  ],
  "explicitLimitsAndUnfinished": [
    "Jar lifetime and matching remain the existing JVM per-session RFC URL/domain/path/scheme model, not original Android registrable-domain Room + session cache + WebView. Bare domain strings are explicitly unsupported here; absolute HTTP(S) URLs are required.",
    "set/remove operate only on cookies returned by the existing jar for that URL/domain and scheme. For example HTTP operations do not delete an HTTPS-only Secure cookie. Original CookieStore persistent-vs-server-session overwrite behavior is not reproduced.",
    "Merge preserves old security/expiration attributes deliberately. This differs from flattening all original CookieStore values into one registrable-domain string; existing attributes are not silently weakened.",
    "Full getCookie text follows the existing JDK request header representation, including RFC2965 attributes/quoting where present. Logical get(url,key) resolves raw values. Original getKey/url additional session-cache lookup is not available.",
    "Original over-4096 random-key deletion, Android Room persistence, shared registrable-domain semantics, WebView cookies and background/login persistence adapters remain unimplemented.",
    "RuleSource loginHeader/source variables/cache are not yet unified with the RuntimeSession stores; this only connects its cookie access. Full AnalyzeUrl, WebBook search/detail/TOC/content and pagination/batch product routing remain unfinished.",
    "Environment closure rejects later operations but does not clear shared jar/cancel another task. This synchronous operation does not add an environment cancellation protocol beyond existing lifetime checks.",
    "Windows JDK21 only; no Android/iOS/JNI/Zero/device execution, signing, installation or automatic renewal acceptance."
  ],
